      "name": "Mouse Escape Tarkov",
      "slug": "mouse-escape-tarkov",
      "teaser": "A simple plugin that lets you press a configurable key (default F11) to temporarily disable the mouse cursor locking so you can move you mouse out of the main Tarkov window. This is useful for multi-monitor setups.",
      "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/2755.png",
      "downloads": 966,
      "favourites_count": 0,
      "description": "<p>A simple plugin that lets you press a configurable key (default F11) to temporarily disable the mouse cursor locking so you can move you mouse out of the main Tarkov window. This is useful for multi-monitor setups.</p>\n<p>This was created expressly to make playing on linux less unbearable. There are other tweaks to make things more stable in conjunction with this (I know I was getting some crashing before made some changes.) Check out the Github for a more detailed guide on some additional tweaks that may help stablaize Tarkov on Linux especially when using this plugin.</p>\n<p>Warning. I wanted this quickly and was lazy because while I’ve worked with Harmony I’ve never done a BepInEx mod so I threw the request to ChatGPT and let it generate the actual code.</p>\n",
